---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
// Traducción de cortesía; el texto vinculante es la versión española.
---
<Base
  title="Cookie policy · Pipilacha"
  description="What cookies pipilacha.es uses, what for, and how to accept, decline or change your choice at any time."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <div class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal information</p>
      <h1 class="reveal-head">Cookie policy</h1>
      <p>What we use, what for, and how to change your choice whenever you like. The binding text is the <a href="/cookies/">Spanish version</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal__body">
      <section>
        <h2>1. What a cookie is</h2>
        <p>A cookie is a small file a site stores on your device to make something work or to remember a choice. Not all of them need permission: strictly technical ones are exempt; the rest only load if you accept them.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. What we use on pipilacha.es</h2>
        <p>Little, and we tell you all of it. We use no advertising cookies. Analytics (Google) cookies load only if you accept them.</p>

        <h3>Technical (necessary, always on)</h3>
        <table class="legal__table">
          <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Source</th><th>What for</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>pipilacha_consent_v1</td>
              <td>Own</td>
              <td>Remember your cookie choice so we don't ask again</td>
              <td>Persistent (until you delete it)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="legal__note">It is stored in your browser's local storage, is not sent to any server and is exempt from consent as it is strictly necessary.</p>

        <h3>Booking — TheFork (third party, only if you accept)</h3>
        <table class="legal__table">
          <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>What for</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>TheFork (thefork.com)</td>
              <td>Load and run the booking calendar on the "Book" page</td>
              <td>Per TheFork (session and persistent)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="legal__note">The TheFork widget does not load —nor set its cookies— until you accept this category. TheFork acts as controller or processor depending on the case; see its own privacy and cookie policy at <a href="https://www.thefork.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">thefork.es</a>.</p>

        <h3>Analytics — Google Analytics (third party, only if you accept)</h3>
        <table class="legal__table">
          <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Source</th><th>What for</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>_ga</td>
              <td>Google (google-analytics.com)</td>
              <td>Distinguish visitors to count visits and page views, in aggregate</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>_ga_*</td>
              <td>Google (google-analytics.com)</td>
              <td>Keep the state of the measurement session</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="legal__note">Google Analytics does not load —nor set its cookies— until you accept this category; if you withdraw it, we stop measuring and delete its cookies. Data is handled in aggregate to know how many people visit us and which pages they look at. Google LLC acts as processor; see its policy at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. How you accept or decline</h2>
        <p>The first time you visit we show a notice to accept, decline or open preferences. Declining is as easy as accepting. If you decline the booking ones, the site still works; you'll just book by phone instead of here.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Change your choice</h2>
        <p>You can change it whenever you like: <button type="button" class="legal__link-btn" data-cc-open>open cookie preferences</button>. You can also delete cookies from your browser settings (Chrome, Safari, Firefox and Edge explain how in their help).</p>
      </section>

      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: July 2026.</p>
      <p class="legal__more">See also <a href="/en/aviso-legal/">Legal notice</a> and <a href="/en/privacidad/">Privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
